-- V145__seed_fravega.sql: Fravega, VTEX: seed plus the curated leaf mapping and the sub-category of each leaf.
--
-- Fravega (www.fravega.com), appliances and electronics department store on VTEX. Only what Fravega itself sells is read: VtexPage filters
-- sellerId 1 (AjustesVtex) and prunes the Servicios and junk nodes before counting, so the catalog is about 3,480 products on 366 leaves,
-- not the 409k rows the legacy API lists (marketplace sellers) nor the 46,702 Plan Canje services. Mixed: rubro_forzado stays NULL (RubroResolver
-- decides by category) and rubro_por_defecto = 'electrodomesticos', like Cetrogar (V139), for what no category decides.
--
-- Leaf mapping: 360 of the 366 leaves carry a category (no new categories; V144 added Artículo de Bebé, Salud and Librería). The curated leaf
-- outranks the name (NormalizerService.SITIOS_DONDE_LA_HOJA_GANA). Fravega abbreviates its names ("FREI.", "LAV."), so the leaf also gives the
-- sub_categoria (V144, read only when the row ends in the leaf's category and the name gave none); a blank sub is NULL, never a sentinel.
-- The six leaves with no category (a gaming PC bucket, garden accessories, door intercoms, camping accessories and lanterns, a "NO USAR" junk leaf) get no row: the name decides.
-- One single-line text blob (sitio_key|origen_id|nombre|categoria|sub rows joined by ';', no raw newline: Sonar flags one inside a literal)
-- split by the INSERT, not a literal per row: a string repeated three times is Sonar S1192, and a long VALUES list of near-identical tuples is
-- what Sonar CPD reads as duplicated code. Regenerated from odd/baselines/site-fravega/leaf_map_reviewed.tsv (leaf_map_final.tsv with 13 leaves corrected by hand).
INSERT INTO sitio (nombre, sitio_key, plataforma, es_premium, rubro_forzado, origen) VALUES
    ('Fravega', 'fravega', 'vtex', false, NULL, 'config')
ON CONFLICT (nombre) DO NOTHING;

